.\" overwrites it.
.SH AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
An auth on action policy can ask for a login again before these actions.
See
.B Auth On Action Policy
in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
A script has the hooks every object type has, and these; a command of another name is in brackets:
.RS
.PP
.na
.nh
add_sign, del_sign, dump, set_config_parameter\ (config), sign.
.hy
.ad
.RE
.\" END AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
.SH FILES
.na
.nh
.TP
\fI/etc/otpme/scripts/\fR
On a node: the scripts a new site gets, one script per file, in the unit \fBscripts\fR.
.TP
\fI/var/lib/otpme/tree/\fR
The objects of the realm.
A script is the directory \fI<name>.script\fR in the directory of its unit, e.g. \fI<realm>.realm/<site>.site/scripts.unit/key_script.sh.script/\fR, with its content and signatures in \fIobject.json\fR, the content encrypted.
It is synced to the nodes only, not to the hosts.
Change it with the commands above, not in the file.
.TP
\fI/var/cache/otpme/offline/<user_uuid>/scripts/\fR
On a host: the scripts of a user as the last login brought them, with their signatures: \fBlogin.script\fR, \fBkey.script\fR and \fBssh\-agent.script\fR.
.TP
\fI~/.otpme/edit/\fR
The file \fBedit\fR opens in your editor.
.hy
